# Git Workflow

## Never push

**Never run `git push` (or any command that pushes to a remote, e.g. `gh pr create` after pushing, `git push --force`, pushing tags) — not even if explicitly asked to "push" or "commit and push".**

- Commits may be created locally when requested.
- After committing, stop and tell the user the commit is ready locally — let the user push themselves.
- If asked to open a PR, prepare the branch/commit locally and ask the user to push first.
